===Pronoun===
{{en-pron|desc=referring to the person being spoken to, previously mentioned|the reflexive case of|you}}

# {{lb|en|reflexive pronoun}} Your [[own]] [[self]] (singular).
#: {{ux|en|Be careful with that fire or you'll burn '''yourself'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|After a good night's sleep you'll feel like '''yourself''' again.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Madeline Holcombe|title=It might be time to ‘reparent’ yourself. Here’s how to get started|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/28/health/reparenting-yourself-how-to-start-wellness|date=2025-04-28|passage=As an adult, you would find '''yourself''' being a people pleaser with the men in your life –– afraid to be rejected and emotionally abandoned.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251114020204/https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/28/health/reparenting-yourself-how-to-start-wellness|archivedate=14 November 2025}}
# {{lb|en|[[emphatic pronoun]]}} {{U|you}} (singular); {{non-gloss|used emphatically, especially to indicate exclusiveness of the referent's participation in the predicate, i.e., that no one else is involved}}.
#: {{ux|en|You '''yourself''' know that what you wrote was wrong.}}
# {{lb|en|especially|Ireland|;|proscribed<ref>https://brians.wsu.edu/2016/05/19/yourself/</ref>}} [[you|You]] (singular); {{non-gloss|even when "you" has not been used previously; see usage notes}}.
#: {{ux|en|I spoke with '''yourself''' last in February.}}
#: {{ux|en|No one understands me like '''yourself'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|My colleague and '''yourself''' are invited to the conference.}}
#: {{ux|en|I only spoke to my lawyer and '''yourself''' about the issue.}}
# Oneself.
#: {{ux|en|These days you have to watch '''yourself''' in the center of the city.}}

====Usage notes====
Use of "yourself" as in "I spoke with yourself last in February." is an untriggered reflexive (i.e. "yourself" is used to mean "you" without the pronoun "you" being used previously in the sentence), which is proscribed.

